summary:
  A park leaves the heal clock running, so the recovery road keeps working on a
  station the listener has already silenced.

history:
  The root of the whole family. A full stop silences thirteen things; a park
  silenced three, and every way a parked room woke up ran on one of the ten
  left behind — the heal ladder on its own timers, the search preview on a
  directory reply already on the wire, the bitrate fallback on a pending 600 ms
  retry. Each was found and closed one at a time over two releases, which is
  exactly how a list like that grows. The park now inherits the stop's
  teardown, and the invariant compares the two sides rather than naming roads,
  so a timer added to one and forgotten on the other fails the gate instead of
  a listener's evening.

target:
  package/contents/ui/main.qml

find:
          healTimer.stop();
          healRetryTimer.stop();

replace:
          healRetryTimer.stop();
          healRetryTimer.stop();

expect:
  Killed by tests/test_invariants.py::test_a_park_inherits_the_stops_teardown.
  Line-neutral.
